Based on your description, it seems you're looking for a script to implement a rate-limiting strategy to prevent excessive requests to a website or service, which can be similar to a Denial of Service (DoS) attack. Here's a simple and basic Python script using a common rate-limit strategy - utilizing a dictionary to store and manage request counts.

```python
import time

class RateLimiter:
    def __init__(self, max_requests_per_second = 10):
        self.max_requests_per_second = max_requests_per_second
        self.requests = {}

    def is_allowed(self, client_ip):
        current_time = int(time.time())
        elapsed_time = current_time - self.requests.get(client_ip, current_time)

        if len(self.requests) >= self.max_requests_per_second:
            time_left = 1 / self.max_requests_per_second - elapsed_time / 60.0
            seconds_left = round(time_left, 2)
            return False, f"Too many requests in the last 60 seconds. Try again in {seconds_left} seconds."

        self.requests[client_ip] = current_time
        return True


